# PORT sprint (`start`)

Jira: site `https://shubhamshindeinbox.atlassian.net`, project **PORT**.
GitHub: PRs target **main**. Reviewer: **Shubham-code-lab** (PR body only; do not use `--reviewer` on their own PRs).

Jira/GitHub **how** (batching, working JQL, failed `gh` calls): [port-jira-github-playbook.mdc](port-jira-github-playbook.mdc).

## Jira links (always)

Every mention of a ticket in chat, PR title/body, and Jira comments must be a markdown link:

`[PORT-13](https://shubhamshindeinbox.atlassian.net/browse/PORT-13)`

Never write bare `PORT-13` as the only reference.

## Sprint gate (do not skip)

Only implement tickets that are **already in the sprint** (active or future). Backlog is not work.

If the user asks to code or open a PR for something that is **not** in the sprint:

1. **Stop.** Tell them it is backlog, name the ticket as a link, and ask them to move it into the sprint.
2. Do **not** create a new ticket and start it in the same turn.
3. Do **not** start the work until the next `start` (or they confirm it is in the sprint).

`start` with an empty sprint: say so and stop. Do not invent PORT-14-style work from the backlog.

## When the user says `start`

Do this in order. Do not skip Jira.

1. Read sprint work with JQL:
   `project = PORT AND (sprint in openSprints() OR sprint in futureSprints())`
   Dragging a ticket onto a sprint on the backlog puts it in a **future** sprint. `openSprints()` only matches after **Start sprint**. Always include `futureSprints()` so planned sprint work is not missed.
2. If that query is empty, stop and say so. Do not pull from backlog.
3. Implement the sprint work (one ticket at a time unless they say otherwise).
4. Open a PR to **main**. Assign/request review from **Shubham-code-lab**. If GitHub blocks self-review, still @ them in the PR body as the reviewer.
5. On the Jira ticket: add a **worklog**, comment with the PR URL, move to **In Progress** (or **Done** only if they asked).
6. Update [`release.json`](release.json): add the ticket key to `tickets`. Do **not** bump `version` or set `publish: true` unless they asked.
7. Related follow-ups: create backlog tickets, **link** them to the current issue, leave them in backlog. Unrelated extras: create in backlog or list them; do not implement.
8. Cap **new** tickets this run at **10** total. Never create tickets in a loop.

## `release.json`

```json
{
  "version": "1.0.1",
  "description": "…",
  "publish": false,
  "tickets": ["PORT-7"]
}
```

`tickets` is the list of Jira keys in this unreleased work.

## Do not

- Implement backlog-only items, even if the user also says “raise a PR” for a file. Tell them first; wait until that ticket is in the sprint.
- Merge the PR (they review and approve).
- Create more than 10 new issues per `start`.
- Set `publish: true` just because a ticket finished.
